course: dictionary
lesson: 14178
title: Momma and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound different in different places, but they still mean something clear. Momma is an informal word, mainly used in the United States. It is a child's word for their mother, a bit like Mum or Mom. «My momma packed my lunch before school.» The words around momma tell you the speaker is close to their mother.
explain: Momma can also mean any mother, even an animal's mother. «The momma bear walked slowly, with her two cubs behind her.» Here momma does not mean one child's own mum. It means the mother bear. Nature books often say momma bird or momma cat for the same reason.
explain: Some people use momma as slang in jokes. A «momma's boy» is a boy who relies on his mother a lot. Jokes that begin "Yo momma" tease someone about their mother, and they are often unkind. Context tells you which meaning is which, so read the words around the word before you decide.
fact: «Momma» is an informal word, mainly used in the United States.
fact: «Momma» means Mom, a child's word for their mother.
fact: «Momma» can mean any mother, including an animal, as in «momma bear».
fact: A «momma's boy» is a boy who relies on his mother a lot.
fact: «Yo momma» jokes tease someone about their mother, and they are often unkind, so think before you use them.
exercise: «My momma packed my lunch before school.» What does momma mean here? | A baby sister | A teacher | *Mom | A grandmother
exercise: What does momma mean in «the momma cat»? | A grey kitten | *The mother cat | A cat that is sleeping | A cat with no kittens
exercise: Which phrase describes a boy who relies on his mother a lot? | *Momma's boy | Yo momma | Momma bird | Momma bear
test: Which sentence uses momma to mean a mother animal? | «Momma, can I have a biscuit?» | *«The momma elephant led the herd to the river.» | «Yo momma is so funny.» | «My momma is making tea in the kitchen.»
test: Why might a writer use momma in a story set in the southern USA? | To tell the reader the story is set in Japan | To explain how to bake a cake | To show the speaker is a maths teacher | *To show a warm, homely voice from the southern USA
exam: What is a «Yo momma» joke? | A recipe for pancakes | A sad poem about a lost cat | *A slang joke that teases someone about their mother | A song about a bear
